<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 15px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # 2 – Lesson # 2</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 2</p></td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Reading</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Grade:</b> 6th Grade (CEFR: A2.1)</p></td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Scenario:</b> Our Community News</p></td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Theme:</b> Reporting From the School!</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</p></td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Reading: reading_1: Identify specific information from fictional short texts. reading_2: Identify the sequence of events in simple stories. phonemic_awareness: Demonstrate knowledge of phonemic awareness by identifying short and long vowel sounds in orally stated single-syllable words.</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Reading: Can identify specific information about community events in short fictional texts (e.g., 'The school organized a fair last week.' 'The community held a clean-up day at the park.'). Can recognize the sequence of events in simple stories about community traditions (e.g., Students read a story about the Desfile de las Mil Polleras and identify the order of events: 'First, the participants gathered, then the parade started, and finally, they celebrated with music and food.'). Can identify short and long vowel sounds in words related to community events (e.g., recognizing /æ/ in 'banner' vs. /eɪ/ in 'parade' or /ɪ/ in 'tradition' vs. /iː/ in 'queen' when reading about local celebrations).</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="background-color: #f2f2f2;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; text-align: left; color: #1a5276; width: 30%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; text-align: left; color: #1a5276; width: 50%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; text-align: left; color: #1a5276; width: 20%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0 0 5px 0;">STAGE 1</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up / Pre-task</b><br>(Engagement, Modeling and Clarification)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays pictures of different community events and school activities (e.g., a school fair, a clean-up day, a traditional parade, a school mural project). Students identify the events and recall vocabulary from Lesson 1, such as 'festival', 'parade', 'mural', 'community fair', 'celebrate'. The teacher asks: "What did you see in the pictures? What events happened in our community last year?"</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher writes a simple sentence on the board using past simple tense and target vocabulary: "Last week, our school <b>prepared</b> a beautiful <b>mural</b>." The teacher models reading the sentence aloud, pointing to each word. The teacher also models the pronunciation of key words, especially focusing on short and long vowel sounds (e.g., /æ/ in 'banner' vs. /eɪ/ in 'parade', /ɪ/ in 'tradition' vs. /iː/ in 'queen') and past tense -ed endings (/d/ in 'prepared').</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Did the school prepare the mural today or last week?" (Checks understanding of past tense).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Is a 'mural' a drawing on a wall or a small photo?" (Checks vocabulary understanding).</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 min</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0 0 5px 0;">STAGE 2</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Presentation</b><br>(Input of new language/content)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short fictional news report text titled "Our School Fair Was a Great Success!" or "Community Clean-up Day". The text, adapted for A2.1, will describe a recent school or community event using past simple tense, compound sentences with 'but', descriptive adjectives (e.g., 'colorful', 'friendly', 'tall'), and target vocabulary (e.g., 'community fair', 'reporter', 'participated', 'prepared', 'celebrated', 'market', 'banner'). It will also describe an artisan or community member. Example text fragment: "Last Saturday, our school hosted its annual community fair. Many students and teachers <b>participated</b>. We saw a <b>colorful</b> banner at the entrance. Mr. Ricardo, a local <b>artisan</b> with <b>curly hair</b>, sold his traditional crafts. I liked the delicious food, but I didn't like the long lines."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Reads and understands main ideas and specific information in short, simple fictional texts about familiar topics.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
                <ol>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist question:</b> Students read the text silently. The teacher asks, "What is this news report mainly about?" (e.g., a school fair, a clean-up day). Students select the best answer from options or provide a short oral answer.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False statements:</b> Students read the text again and decide if statements are True or False. Examples: "The fair was on Sunday." (False) "Mr. Ricardo sold crafts." (True) "The reporter liked the long lines." (False, checking understanding of 'but' clause).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Information Matching:</b> Students match specific details from the text to questions (Who, What, Where, When). Example: Match "Last Saturday" with "When was the fair?". Match "Mr. Ricardo" with "Who was the artisan?".</li>
                </ol>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10-12 min</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0 0 5px 0;">STAGE 3</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Preparation / Practice</b><br>(Accuracy focus on Reading)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Identifying specific information and sequence of events from texts; practicing past simple tense, compound sentences with 'but', descriptive adjectives, and target vocabulary. Demonstrating knowledge of short and long vowel sounds.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ol>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Controlled Practice - Gap Fill:</b> The teacher provides a worksheet with sentences from the news report text, but with key verbs (in past simple) or vocabulary words missing. Students fill in the blanks by referring back to the text. Example: "Many students and teachers ____ (participate) in the fair." "Mr. Ricardo, a local ____ (artisan/reporter), sold crafts."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Semi-controlled Practice - Vowel Sound Sort:</b> The teacher displays a list of words from the text (e.g., 'banner', 'parade', 'tradition', 'queen', 'fair', 'met'). Students work in pairs to identify and underline the short or long vowel sound in each word. The teacher then guides a class check, having students say the words and identify the sound, focusing on /æ/, /eɪ/, /ɪ/, /iː/.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pair Reading & Sequencing:</b> The teacher gives pairs short paragraphs or jumbled sentences from a simple story about a community tradition (e.g., "First, the participants gathered. Then, the parade started. Finally, they celebrated with music and food."). Students read the parts and work together to put the events in the correct sequence, then read the sequenced story aloud to each other. They highlight words showing sequence like 'first', 'then', 'finally'.</li>
                </ol>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">15-18 min</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0 0 5px 0;">STAGE 4</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Performance / Production</b><br>(Communicative task)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task format:</b> "Community News Reporter Teams"</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students work in small groups (3-4 students). Each group receives a different short fictional text (e.g., a "report" about a school play, a local market, or a small festival). The texts will vary slightly in content but use similar target vocabulary, past simple tense, and include some descriptive adjectives. Groups act as "reporter teams" and their task is to read their assigned text carefully to identify:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What event happened?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">When and where did it happen?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Who participated or was involved?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What was something interesting or unique about the event? (e.g., "The traditional dances were great, but the music was a little loud.")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">If the text describes a sequence, what happened first, next, and last?</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">After reading and discussing, each group prepares to briefly "report" their findings to the class, summarizing the key information they identified from their text. The focus is on their ability to read for specific details and sequence information, and to collaboratively present what they understood from the text.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10 min</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0 0 5px 0;">STAGE 5</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment / Post-task</b><br>(Formative assessment)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative assessment strategy:</b> Teacher Observation Checklist.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students individually read a new short fictional paragraph (2-3 sentences) about a school or community event. They then answer 2-3 short comprehension questions on a slip of paper, requiring them to identify specific information (who, what, when) and put a simple sequence in order if applicable (e.g., "What happened before the band played?").</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Accuracy in identifying specific information (e.g., correct answer to 'who', 'what', 'when').</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Correct sequence of events (if applicable).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Participation and collaboration during group activity (observed).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Demonstrated awareness of vowel sounds in spoken words (observed).</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students answer the following questions on a small paper slip:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was one new thing you learned about reading news stories today?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How easy or difficult was it for you to find specific details in the texts? (Easy / Okay / Difficult)"</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5 min</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0 0 5px 0;">STAGE 6</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Reflection</b></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What part of reading about our community news did I find most interesting today?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is one reading strategy I can use next time to understand a story better?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b> What worked well in this reading lesson? The specific focus on identifying information and sequencing events seemed effective. Students enjoyed the 'reporter teams' activity. Some students still struggled with distinguishing certain short and long vowel sounds, and a few had difficulty with the 'but' clauses in compound sentences. I will need to provide more explicit pronunciation practice for these sounds and extra examples for 'but' in the next lessons, perhaps through targeted listening activities or sentence building during speaking practice. Scaffolds like pre-highlighted key words could be added for struggling readers.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> This reading lesson provided the content and vocabulary for talking about community events. The next lesson (Lesson 3: Speaking & Interaction) will build on this by having students actively share and discuss their interpretations of community news, using the target vocabulary and grammar to express their experiences and preferences.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">3-5 min</p></td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>